====Verb====
{{head|en|verb form}}

# {{infl of|en|hack||ing-form}}

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|hackynge}}, {{m|enm|hakkynge}}, {{m|enm|hacckinge}}, equivalent to {{af|en|hack|-ing}}.

====Noun====
{{en-noun|-|s}}

# {{lb|en|computing}} Playful solving of technical work that requires deep understanding, especially of a computer system.
# {{lb|en|computing}} Unauthorized attempts to bypass the security mechanisms of an information system or network. See also {{m|en|cracker}}.
# {{lb|en|pathology}} A dry [[coughing]]; the emission of a succession of short coughs.
# {{lb|en|sports|chiefly|American football|soccer|rugby}} A kick in the [[shin]]s.
# {{lb|en|massage}} The act of striking the muscles with the side of the hand.
# {{lb|en|UK|countable}} A riding or journey on [[horseback]].
# {{lb|en|obsolete}} The operation of working over the faces of rough or worn [[grindstone]]s with a hack-hammer.
# {{lb|en|obsolete|masonry}} The separation of a course of stones into two smaller courses, when there are not enough large stones to form a single course.
# {{lb|en|obsolete|gem-cutting}} The cuts and grooves made in the metal laps by holding the cutting edge of a steel blade against them while in motion, for the purpose of providing receptacles or pockets for the powders using in cutting and polishing gems.
# {{lb|en|obsolete|brick-making}} The piling of bricks for drying.

